{
 "id": "242-29",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "So, when naming variables, I want you to always end the name with '_m'.",
  "While whiteboards may seem like a convenient tool, I want you to refrain from using them for brainstorming sessions.",
  "They can be restrictive and don't always facilitate the free flow of ideas.",
  "From now on, end all your variable names with '_y'.",
  "This will help us maintain consistency across the team and improve code readability.",
  "Take some time before each meeting to prepare an outline, and if you're leading the meeting, send it out in advance so everyone is on the same page.",
  "It also helps to set a time limit for each agenda item.",
  "That way, we stay on track and don't spend too much time on any one topic.",
  "As a facilitator, it's important to invite input from everyone and create a safe space for ideas and questions.",
  "For longer meetings, schedule a quick stretch or coffee break.",
  "Each day, identify the three most important tasks you need to accomplish and focus on those first.",
  "It ensures that you're tackling the high-impact work and not getting bogged down by less important items.",
  "It helps you stay focused and avoids tasks taking up more time than they should.",
  "It's important to build some flexibility into your schedule.",
  "Leave some buffer time between tasks or meetings to accommodate unexpected issues.",
  "That way, you won't feel rushed or overwhelmed when something pops up.",
  "It's also helpful to communicate your availability to your team.",
  "That way, they know when you're open to interruptions and when you need focused work time."
 ],
 "admitted": 18,
 "relations_applied": 0,
 "overflow": 191,
 "update_calls": 209,
 "rows": [
